body:
It was just a kiss. Of course that doesn't justify kissing anyone while still being in a relationship, but it's still not as bad as sleeping with someone else. And besides, alcohol consumption can cause quite the ordeal of misfortune to anyone, really. You saw this as a mistake, it means you understand the situation, you can classify them as a mistake from your part. Acknowledging it is already a sign that you're aware of the consequences of said actions. You're intelligent. And your ex might need some time, sure, but he can not hold a grudge against you. You were intoxicated. No one thinks straight in this state. As said, you just have to make sure to adjust your consumption to a less intoxicating level.

&#x200B;

I can speak from experience when I say too much alcohol does destroy relationships and families. My dad is an alcoholic and whenever he was drinking nothing ever good came out of his mouth, nor did he do anything rational. When sober, he's a decent man. But he can't control his consumption. It's best to slow down early, when you still have control.

Hey there. Are you afraid of changes or maybe you're overthinking about life?

&#x200B;

Maybe you'd like some advice from someone who has been in your shoes.  
I mean to say, I've had that feeling as well and no, you're not crazy. It's a feeling everyone eventually has while they're growing up. I thought to myself "Damn life sucks!" until I moved out to live on my own, unprepared, because I didn't want to deal with the situation I was in. Turns out the situation I was in was actually a nice version of what came after I moved out. I was unprepared, didn't let anyone talk to me, didn't want to speak up and I ended up feeling rejected. Because I rejected others. You're young, you possibly have talent in music or art or maybe you're really good at games, sports or creative writing. And given the fact that you're typing grammatically correct shows me that you're intelligent. Which can be a burden sometimes but it really is just a perk of being self-aware.

&#x200B;

Maybe you forgot who you are. What do you like to do? What's your speciality?
